# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data (872 MB) -- deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# Everything under data/ is either a user-supplied input or a derived artefact
# that scripts/00_acquire.py and scripts/01_build_db.py rebuild from scratch:
#
#   Ecomics.*.{txt,csv}   the published release (259 MB), from the Ecomics
#                         Dropbox linked at http://prokaryomics.com/download
#   external/             scraped + downloaded resources (189 MB)
#   ecomics.db            the built SQLite compendium (347 MB)
#   parquet/              wide matrices mirrored for fast loading (78 MB)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
data.zip

# Large or regenerable outputs. The per-layer metrics ARE tracked -- they are
# the result of record: pipeline_validation.json, transcriptome_loco.json,
# methods_faithful_eval.json and proteome_loco.json.
results/*.npz
results/*.log
results/*.png

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code not reachable from scripts/ -- kept locally, not published.
#
# This file IS the scope statement for this repository. Adding or removing a
# line here publishes or unpublishes code; it is not housekeeping.
#
#   plots.py, figures/   the figure atlas. Its entry point upstream is
#                        scripts/15_figures.py, which is not part of this
#                        subset, so the registry has no caller here. ~2,375
#                        lines.
#   moma/{fluxome,metabolome,phenome}.py
#                        three of the five omics layers -- the rest of the
#                        paper's cascade beyond the transcriptome and the
#                        proteome. ~1,266 lines.
#
# moma/_lasso.py and moma/proteome.py were published on 2026-08-12 together
# with scripts/04_proteome.py. _lasso.py is shared with the unpublished
# metabolome; it has no reverse dependency on it.
#
# moma/__init__.py stays tracked, and keeps re-exporting ONLY transcriptome:
# Python executes it on any `ecomics.moma.*` import, so a proteome re-export
# there would drag _lasso and sklearn into every transcriptome run. Import the
# proteome from its own module instead.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
ecomics/plots.py
ecomics/figures/
ecomics/moma/fluxome.py
ecomics/moma/metabolome.py
ecomics/moma/phenome.py

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/

# R
.Rhistory
.RData

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.obsidian/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
INFO-CARD.md
docs/04-reproduce.md
